@import copy from '../../components/copy.clarus'
@import docs from '../../layouts/docs.clarus'

<docs [title]="'Inputs'" [path]="'/guide/inputs'" [description]="'Typed inputs with @input, defaults, and types imported with @import type.'">
  <h1>Inputs</h1>
  <p class="lead"><code>@input</code> declares what a component receives, with a TypeScript type and an optional default.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre><code verbatim>@import type { User } from '../domain/user'
@input user: User
@input size: 'sm' | 'lg' = 'sm'

<p class="{{ size }}">{{ user.name }}</p></code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <p>An input with a default is optional. <code>@import type</code> brings in types for inputs; it is erased from the compiled output. <code>clarusjs check</code> verifies every use of a component against its inputs.</p>
</docs>
